# ruby2js-master's own nested .gitignore excludes demo/selfhost/{ruby2js.js,filters/} as
# regeneratable build output, and its own node_modules as an installable dependency - but our
# tools/*.mjs import demo/selfhost/ruby2js.js and demo/selfhost/filters/functions.js directly
# at runtime, and demo/selfhost/node_modules/@ruby/prism (~1.2M) is the Ruby parser ruby2js.js
# loads at runtime. A root-level `!negation` here can't override a NESTED .gitignore (the
# deeper file wins), so those specific paths are `git add -f`orced instead, to keep this repo
# runnable from a fresh clone without a Ruby toolchain.
.aider*
